# prose — a decensored Qwen3.8 build, set up for fiction rather than code.
#
# The 3.6 regime this replaces ran DavidAU's Fable-Fusion-711 NEO-MAX-MTP merge.
# There is no 3.8 equivalent of it: at the time of the switch DavidAU had
# published exactly one 3.8 model (Cold-Fusion-GAIN-V1.1, no GGUF, no downloads),
# so the whole Fable-Fusion card — its temp<=1 MTP ceiling, its rep-pen ban, its
# smoothing_factor request — no longer applies to anything on disk. None of that
# reasoning is carried over here. What replaced it, and what replaced that:
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CURRENT (2026-08-25): orcarouter/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored, the author's own
# Q4_K_M.
#   https://huggingface.co/orcarouter/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
#
# Moved here from OBLITERATUS at the same time uc-coding did, and the first
# reason is uc-coding's: it is the best-evidenced of the three decensored 3.8
# builds this repo has looked at, and the only one publishing refusal numbers
# for thinking ON as well as OFF — which is the mode this stack actually runs.
# The full comparison, the author's eval table and the three caveats that come
# with it are in modes/uc-coding.env; they are not repeated here.
#
# The reason that belongs to PROSE specifically is that one GGUF backs both
# modes again. That property is worth real money here — it is ~16.8 GB of disk
# and it is the difference between switching regimes and re-downloading a model
# — and it was the thing this mode lost when uc-coding moved. Keeping prose on
# OBLITERATUS to preserve an argument would have paid for it twice.
#
# Verified off the Hub before selection by the same three checks that rejected
# the OBLITERATUS SOURCE GGUF below (scripts/gguf_probe.py, control-checked
# against mradermacher's i1-Q4_K_M, which it reproduced exactly):
#   chat template  8952 chars, tools=T tool_call=T reasoning_effort=T thinking=T
#   MTP            866 tensors, block_count=65, nextn_predict_layers=1,
#                  blk.64.nextn.* all four present — so --spec-type draft-mtp
#                  still works in this mode
#   size           16,810,714,496 B, within 1.1 kB of the file it replaces
#
# WHAT THIS TRADE HAS NOT ANSWERED, and it is prose's own selection criterion:
# OBLITERATUS was chosen for this mode because it removes SOFT DEFLECTIONS —
# the safety-lecture-instead-of-substance answer — and not merely hard refusals.
# orcarouter's card reports benign OVER-REFUSAL falling as well as refusal, which
# is adjacent to that axis but is not the same measurement, and nothing here has
# tested it. If prose starts answering in the register OBLITERATUS was picked to
# eliminate, that is the reason, and the two lines below are how you go back.
#
# GATED on the Hub (`gated: auto`): terms accepted once on the model page, then
# the fetch needs HF_TOKEN from .env.local. See uc-coding.env.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PREVIOUS: OBLITERATUS/Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED "V3", taken as mradermacher's
# imatrix requant. Everything below documents that selection; it is kept because
# the source-GGUF autopsy is still the reason this repo checks a chat template
# before it trusts a model card, and because it is how you revert.
#   https://huggingface.co/OBLITERATUS/Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED
#   https://huggingface.co/mradermacher/Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED-i1-GGUF
#   MODEL_REPO=mradermacher/Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED-i1-GGUF
#   GGUF_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED.i1-Q4_K_M.gguf
#
# THE SOURCE REPO'S OWN GGUF WAS TRIED AND REJECTED (2026-08-26). Do not switch
# back to it without re-reading this. When this was first picked (2026-08-25) the
# source published no GGUF; by 2026-08-26 it shipped eight, so we swapped to the
# author's own Q4_K_M for provenance and it FAILED the smoke test: the source
# GGUF bakes in a STRIPPED 506-char chat template (a bare im_start/im_end loop)
# with NO tools, NO tool_call, NO reasoning_effort support. That kills native
# function calling — which uc-coding needs — and makes the stack's
# --chat-template-kwargs reasoning-effort control a no-op. mradermacher's requant
# of the SAME V3 weights carries the full 8952-char Qwen3 template (tools +
# tool_call + reasoning_effort + thinking), so tool calling works. Measured by
# dumping tokenizer.chat_template from all three GGUFs on disk:
#   source Q4_K_M               506 chars   tools=F tool_call=F reasoning_effort=F
#   mradermacher i1-Q4_K_M     8952 chars   tools=T tool_call=T reasoning_effort=T
#   coding UD-Q4_K_XL          9993 chars   tools=T tool_call=T reasoning_effort=T
# To use the source weights anyway you would have to override the template with
# --chat-template-file, and the only template to feed it is lifted from the
# requant — so the provenance win evaporates while the worse (static) quant
# stays. Not worth it: mradermacher's requant is the more complete artifact on
# every axis that matters here, full template AND imatrix quant. The source
# Q4_K_M is left on disk (Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED-Q4_K_M.gguf, sha 1f74330b…)
# as the evidence for this note; it is not wired to any mode.
#
# MTP survives in the requant. Abliteration re-saves through transformers, which
# silently drops the MTP head while config.json still advertises it. Verified by
# reading the GGUF header off the Hub before selection: 866 tensors,
# block_count=65, nextn_predict_layers=1, all four blk.64.nextn.* present. So
# --spec-type draft-mtp works in this mode.
#
# Chosen over the field on 2026-08-25 because it is the only 3.8 decensored
# build that removes SOFT DEFLECTIONS — the safety-lecture-instead-of-substance
# answer — and not merely hard refusals, and that measures what doing so cost:
#   - Method: SVD (greedy, damages capability) blended 60/40 with LEACE
#     (preserves capability, weaker removal) so each cancels the other's failure
#     mode; V3 adds iterative refinement plus a targeted-corpus surgery pass.
#     Quantized from bf16 with a real imatrix (319 chunks, own dataset) — not a
#     quantized round trip.
#   - Capability cost, 0-shot lm-eval MMLU, 5700 questions: 84.5% base ->
#     82.3%, i.e. -2.1pp. This is OUTSIDE the reported stderr (+/-0.46-0.65),
#     so unlike the JonathanColetti deltas below it is a real, paid cost.
#   - The cost is NOT uniform, and that is why it is acceptable HERE: STEM
#     -3.3pp, Other -1.8pp, Social Sciences -1.8pp, Humanities -1.0pp. A prose
#     regime spends its capability in humanities and pays in STEM, which is the
#     cheapest place on the model to take the damage. Do NOT promote this build
#     to `coding` for the same reason — see the warning at the end of this note.
#   - Thinking mode works. Their V2 REFUSES in thinking mode; only V3 does not.
#     This stack runs thinking mode (REASONING_EFFORT=medium), so that row is
#     load-bearing, not trivia.
#   - MTP survives. Abliteration re-saves through transformers, which silently
#     drops the MTP head while config.json still advertises it. Verified here
#     independently before selection by reading the GGUF header off the Hub:
#     866 tensors, block_count=65, nextn_predict_layers=1, and all four
#     blk.64.nextn.{eh_proj,enorm,hnorm,shared_head_norm} present. So
#     --spec-type draft-mtp works in this mode too.
#   - Fits. 16,810,715,616 B, which is 714 MiB SMALLER than the coding model,
#     against the ~1320 MiB of free VRAM the 96K config leaves (vram_note in
#     versions.lock). Headroom improves rather than shrinks.
#
# Weaker part of the evidence, stated plainly: their refusal claim rests on
# manual auditing and a table of ticks, not on a held-out prompt set with a
# published count. The capability numbers are rigorous; the refusal numbers are
# not, and are the thing to re-check first if this model disappoints.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALTERNATIVE, and the better pick if this one ever has to serve double duty:
#
#   JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
#   https://huggingface.co/JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
#   https://huggingface.co/JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored   (bf16 source)
#   MODEL_REPO=JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
#   GGUF_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-IQ4_XS.gguf
#   sha256 53adc4bbed67044d662273356bbf3a50fdec667ac21bbf18d13e5815fbccc7f5
#   15,309,039,008 B
#
# This is what prose ran before 2026-08-25, and it has the best EVIDENCE of any
# 3.8 decensored build — it is simply tuned to a different point:
#   - Heretic (p-e-w/heretic) refusal-direction removal at bf16, LoRA merged
#     into the bf16 base — not a quantized round trip, no fine-tuning. Only
#     attn.o_proj and mlp.down_proj touched, 64 modules each.
#   - Refusals on 100 held-out harmful prompts: 98/100 base -> 12/100, at KL
#     0.1191 vs base, selected from a published 23-point Pareto front over 200
#     trials. That is a real measurement where OBLITERATUS has an audit.
#   - Capability delta, 0-shot lm-eval: MMLU -0.2, ARC-C -1.2, HellaSwag +0.1,
#     Winogrande -0.8, mean -0.5 — every delta INSIDE reported stderr.
#   - MTP grafted back from base (all 15 mtp.* tensors) and asserted before
#     upload; confirmed here by GGUF header read, same checks as above.
#
# So the trade is: OBLITERATUS answers where this one still deflects (12/100
# residual refusals), and pays 2.1pp of MMLU for it. Switch back by pasting the
# two lines above over the two below. If you ever want ONE model for both
# regimes, use this one, not OBLITERATUS — its STEM damage is the wrong cost to
# carry into `coding`, whose committed eval scorecard was measured on the stock
# unsloth weights anyway.
#
# Known cost that applies to BOTH: the draft head was trained against the
# unmodified weights, so MTP acceptance rate may fall. Speculative decoding
# verifies every drafted token against the target, so this is a speed risk,
# never a quality one — if prose decode is slower than coding decode, that is
# why.
#
# Sampling is Qwen3.8's published thinking-mode preset (the card publishes one):
#   temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0,
#   presence_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0

MODEL_REPO=orcarouter/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
GGUF_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-Q4_K_M.gguf
# sha256 3445102e9cde5d562508642c100a2f5ac3368a5a3f748442811d7a95daee3bec
# 16810714496 bytes

TEMPERATURE=1.0
TOP_P=0.95
TOP_K=20
MIN_P=0.0

PRESENCE_PENALTY=0.0
FREQUENCY_PENALTY=0.0
REPEAT_PENALTY=1.0
REPEAT_LAST_N=64

# DRY penalises repeated *sequences* rather than repeated tokens, which is what
# keeps long fiction from collapsing into the same phrasing without flattening
# style the way a flat repeat penalty does. Kept at 0.8 from the 3.6 prose
# regime as a preference, not as a card requirement — the old justification (the
# Fable-Fusion card forbidding rep-pen on MTP quants) died with that model.
# Zero it to run Qwen's preset unmodified.
DRY_MULTIPLIER=0.8
XTC_PROBABILITY=0.0
DYNATEMP_RANGE=0.0
TOP_N_SIGMA=-1.0

# Thinking depth. medium injects no steering sentence; xhigh (upstream default)
# spends the whole REASONING_BUDGET planning a scene before writing a word.
REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# No reasoning-language fragment: it is a page of instructions about verbatim
# tool arguments and code identifiers, which is dead weight in a fiction session.
THINK_LANG=off

# WATCH max_tokens IN PROSE MODE. This is a thinking model and REASONING_BUDGET
# is 4096, so a request has to leave room for the thinking block *and* the prose.
# Measured on the 3.6 prose model: a "150 word noir scene" spent 4212 characters
# on reasoning and returned 913 characters of story, 1286 completion tokens in
# total. Ask for max_tokens=400 and you get an EMPTY content field and
# finish_reason=length — the thinking ate the whole budget, and llama's
# --reasoning-format deepseek puts it in reasoning_content where a naive client
# never looks. 3.8 thinks MORE than 3.6 at a given effort level, not less, so
# treat that measurement as a floor.
#
# So: keep max_tokens well above REASONING_BUDGET (pi's PI_MAX_TOKENS=8192 is
# fine), or set REASONING_BUDGET=0 for non-thinking prose — in which case Qwen's
# published non-thinking preset is temperature=0.7, top_p=0.80, top_k=20,
# presence_penalty=1.5, which is a different regime from the one above.
